== Adopted conventions and one departure

Two sibling projects served as references: `holy-shit-ios` (SwiftUI) and `holy-shit-api` (Go).
The backend adopts holy-shit-api's toolchain, telemetry package, passkey flow, deploy scripts and
mise tasks almost verbatim. The two code bases are intentionally "kept diffable", so that a fix in
one can be ported to the other. The iOS app adopts holy-shit-ios's `AuthService` and onboarding
flow.

The one intentional departure is the backend *layering*. In holy-shit-api, handlers call sqlc
directly. Code Share places a service layer (business rules, transactions) and a repository layer
(multi-table queries) between the generated handlers and the database. This decision was taken by
the owner before any code was written, on the grounds that the household, key-wrap and sync rules
are too intricate to reside in handlers.

#lesson[A stack is verified from the code, not from its description. The GitHub description of
holy-shit-api stated ASP.NET; the code is Go. The plan adopts conventions from what the repository
actually contains, and `CLAUDE.md` now states this explicitly.]
